WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.801
-Our next guest can be seen
at the Las Vegas Comedy Cellar

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:06.300
February 27th through March 3rd.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.300
Please welcome the very funny
Orlando Leyba.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:14.968
♪♪

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:17.167
-Alright!

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:19.868
Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:22.634
Settle down. Thank you.

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:25.534
I'm happy to be here and not at
home watching "Yellowstone."

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:26.868
Alright.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:28.801
Yeah. I'm tired of feeling like
less of a man

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:30.100
every time that I watch.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.634
Every time I watch.

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:34.267
For those that don't know,
"Yellowstone" is a TV show

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:37.701
about a cattle ranch ran by
"The Bodyguard" himself,

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:39.601
Kevin Costner.

00:00:39.601 --> 00:00:43.534
A man who doesn't want outsiders
moving in, buying up the land,

00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:45.400
and turning it
into a Whole Foods.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.767
That's the plot, I think.

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:48.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:50.567
Alright?
Streaming now on Peacock.

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:58.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:00.467
The acting is great.

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:03.667
But the visuals of "Yellowstone"
are amazing.

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:05.200
I'm in love with Yellowstone.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.601
So imagine my excitement
when my buddy Eric Ladd

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:08.701
invited me to his wedding.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.701
Where? In Yellowstone.
"Are you coming?"

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:12.901
"Oh, I'm there!
I've been watching the show."

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:14.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.734 --> 00:01:18.334
The second I landed, guys,
the second I landed, I got it.

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:21.100
This place was so beautiful,
so majestic.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.300
"Is this Narnia?"
I asked the locals.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:27.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:30.167
I -- I understood Kevin Costner.

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:33.334
Shoot, I became Kevin Costner.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:36.534
By the third day, I was telling
people to get off my land.

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:38.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:40.834
Sure, it was at
the hotel courtyard,

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.167
but that's the way that I felt.

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:45.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:48.400
I couldn't stop saying, "Go on,
get," like my buddy Jimmy.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.534 --> 00:01:53.200
"Go on, get.
Go on -- Go on, get!"

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:57.767
"You go on, get, from that
cucumber water. Go on, get."

00:01:57.767 --> 00:01:59.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:00.934
"You've had enough of
our minerals, sir.

00:02:00.934 --> 00:02:03.400
You've had enough."

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.200
I drove out there.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.934
I got to meet real cowboys and
cowgirls, good people working

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:11.634
the land, riding horses,
feeding America.

00:02:11.634 --> 00:02:14.267
I got to met those people
and they got to meet me.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:17.501
Yeah. With my coffee-house
vibes, you know?

00:02:17.501 --> 00:02:19.467
[ Laughter ]
I introduced myself.

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:21.501
"Hello, guys.
My name is Orlando.

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:23.601
My pronouns are he and him.

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:27.567
Uh, I have an extra iced matcha
latte made with rice milk."

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:28.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.634 --> 00:02:30.267
"It's less aggressive
on your tummy.

00:02:30.267 --> 00:02:33.067
Any takers? Any takers?"

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:34.534
There were no takers.

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:36.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:38.267
But I was so impressed by
these people,

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:40.634
and they were so ready for me
to get off their land.

00:02:40.634 --> 00:02:42.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:45.901
So, I drove. I drove into
Yellowstone, and I saw nature.

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:47.834
I'm a city guy and I saw nature.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:50.868
I saw elks, the real ones with
the coat racks. I saw them.

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:52.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:54.734
I saw bears doing bear stuff.

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:57.968
They waved at me.
They waved for real.

00:02:57.968 --> 00:03:00.601
Ha! I saw bisons.

00:03:00.601 --> 00:03:01.834
Those are real.

00:03:01.834 --> 00:03:03.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:06.567
I thought bisons were made up
like unicorns, but...

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:09.000
There he was, a bison
in the middle of the road

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.868
looking like a bougie cow. Moo.

00:03:10.868 --> 00:03:16.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:17.868
I know.

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:21.334
I see you, bougie cow.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:23.267
People honked at it.

00:03:23.267 --> 00:03:24.701
And I was like, "No, you don't
do that.

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:26.934
You don't -- You don't honk
at a dinosaur."

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:29.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:32.267
I, on the other hand, drove
around it with ease

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:35.200
thanks to my rented Ford F-150.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:40.501
I only say that in hopes of
getting Ford to give me

00:03:40.501 --> 00:03:44.968
a free, fully loaded
F-150 truck.

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:46.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:53.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.267
I drove deeper into Yellowstone

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:57.133
because I had to go see
Old Faithful.

00:03:57.133 --> 00:04:00.133
For those that don't know,
Old Faithful is a thermal geyser

00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:02.734
that shoots water and steam
into the air

00:04:02.734 --> 00:04:05.634
from the middle of the Earth,
"allegedly."

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:08.434
They call it Old Faithful
because it will always go off

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:11.634
right on time,
plus or minus 10 minutes.

00:04:11.634 --> 00:04:14.000
When I got there,
this place was packed.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.300
It was packed with people.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.200
They built a whole visiting
center.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.367
I could tell that something was
about to happen,

00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:20.767
but I was way in the back.

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:22.634
And I said, "I don't want to
miss Old Faithful."

00:04:22.634 --> 00:04:24.400
So I shimmied my way
to the front.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.534
"Excuse me, pardon me,
excuse me.

00:04:26.534 --> 00:04:28.334
Go on, get, lady! Excuse me."

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:31.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:34.100
And Old Faithful
did not let us down.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.334
Did not let us down.

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:38.367
It went right off on time,
plus 10 minutes.

00:04:38.367 --> 00:04:39.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:42.834
And when it went off, it shot
so high into the sky,

00:04:42.834 --> 00:04:44.601
I had to take a step back.

00:04:44.601 --> 00:04:47.334
And I was like, "By God."

00:04:47.334 --> 00:04:50.067
It reminded me of me in my 20s.

00:04:50.067 --> 00:04:51.567
Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:53.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:55.000
That's not me anymore.
Understand that.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.367
That's not me anymore.

00:04:56.367 --> 00:04:59.501
I'm more like Old Dependable.

00:04:59.501 --> 00:05:02.634
Or Old Maybe Later,
plus or minus 10 days.

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:07.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:07.534 --> 00:05:09.167
Alright.

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:11.701
I'm going to "go on, get," now.

00:05:11.701 --> 00:05:14.234
I'm Orlando. Thank you.
I'm Orlando Leyba.

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:15.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:15.601 --> 00:05:21.434
♪♪

00:05:21.434 --> 00:05:23.133
-Orlando Leyba!

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:24.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:25.701
Oh, fantastic, buddy.

00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:27.868
He'll be at the Las Vegas
Comedy Cellar

00:05:27.868 --> 00:05:30.501
February 27th through March 3rd.

00:05:30.501 --> 00:05:31.968
We'll be right back, everybody.

